    "diagnosis": "Werner syndrome (WS) clinical appearance and disease progression",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<strong>A,B</strong>&nbsp;A patient with WS originally reported in Epstein et al. {696} illustrates rapid acquisition of features of advanced chronological age from the age of 15&nbsp;years&nbsp;(<strong>A</strong>) to 48&nbsp;years&nbsp;(<strong>B</strong>). Note the rounded face; sharp features; greying, thinning, and loss of scalp and eyebrow hair; and thin, atrophic arms. <strong>C,D</strong>&nbsp;An unrelated patient with WS is shown, at about age 13&nbsp;years after growth had ceased at age 12&nbsp;years&nbsp;(<strong>C</strong>), and at age 56&nbsp;years (<strong>D</strong>). Note the rapid change in appearance over time, sparse hair, thick glasses after cataract surgery, and thin limbs with a bandaged, ulcerated right elbow.",
    "source": "",
